# novadeck uhid access — only while this device hosts a stream.
#
# The sunshine package opens /dev/uhid to group `input` and to the session (60-sunshine.rules), at every
# boot. Whoever can open it can create an input device with any descriptor, which the kernel's HID
# drivers then parse. Only a host needs it, for its guests' gamepads: novadeck-sunshine.service opens it
# for deck when it starts and closes it when it stops.
#
# After 60-sunshine.rules, and before 73-seat-late.rules, which is what acts on the uaccess tag.
# A udev change event on the node while hosting would reset MODE, and with it the access the service gave.
# Nothing here sends one; restarting the host gives it back.
# /dev/uinput stays open: Steam Input needs it (70-novadeck-uinput.rules).
KERNEL=="uhid", GROUP="root", MODE="0600", TAG-="uaccess"
